{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Glimpse of Japan: Cherry Blossoms and Neon Lights**\n\nThis spring, I embarked on a journey to Japan, a country where tradition and modernity coexist seamlessly. My adventure began in Tokyo, where I marveled at the towering skyscrapers of Shinjuku and the serene beauty of Meiji Shrine. The juxtaposition of these two worlds was mesmerizing—lantern-lit torii gates standing tall amidst urban hustle.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the Shinkansen to Kyoto, the cultural heart of Japan. Wandering through the bamboo groves of Arashiyama, I felt a sense of tranquility wash over me. The Fushimi Inari Shrine’s endless tunnels of vermilion torii gates left me in awe, each one bearing the name of a generous donor.\n\nBut the true magic of Japan unfolded in Hiroshima. Standing at the Peace Memorial Park, I reflected on the city’s resilience and the power of peace. A short ferry ride to Miyajima Island revealed the iconic floating torii gate of Itsukushima Shrine, partially submerged at high tide—a sight that seemed almost surreal.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without indulging in its culinary delights. From savory ramen in Kyoto to fresh sushi in Tokyo, every meal was an adventure. I even tried my hand at making soba noodles in a local workshop—a humbling experience!\n\nAs my journey concluded, I left with a heart full of memories and a promise to return. Japan’s blend of ancient traditions and cutting-edge innovation is a testament to its enduring charm. Whether it’s the delicate petals of cherry blossoms or the glow of neon signs, this country captivates the soul.\n\nUntil next time, Japan—arigatou gozaimashita!", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.07776619493961334}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.060129035264253616}, {"token": " Gl", "logprob": -2.946326971054077}, {"token": "imp", "logprob": -1.9073468138230965e-06}, {"token": "se", "logprob": -5.